window.QB_MATHS_QBTEST = {"subject":"DP Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches","level":"SL","topic":{"number":4,"title":"Statistics and probability"},"exercises":[{"id":"19M.1.SL.TZ2.T_6","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"19M","date":"May 2019","tz":"TZ2","legacy":"T_","marks":2,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>A health inspector analysed the amount of sugar in 500 different snacks prepared in various school cafeterias. The collected data are shown in the following box-and-whisker diagram.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p class=\"center\">Amount of sugar per snack in grams</p><p>The health inspector visits two school cafeterias. She inspects the same number of meals at each cafeteria. The data is shown in the following box-and-whisker diagrams.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>Meals prepared in the school cafeterias are required to have less than 10 grams of sugar.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":2,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>State, giving a reason, which school cafeteria has more meals that do not meet the requirement.</p>","ms":"<p>Cafeteria 2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)(C1)</strong></em></p><p>75 % &gt; 50 % (do not meet the requirement)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(R1)(C1)</strong></em></p><p><strong>OR</strong></p><p>25 % &lt; 50 % (meet the requirement)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(R1)(C1)</strong></em></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Do not award (A1)(R0). Award the (R1) for a correct comparison of percentages for both cafeterias, which may be in words. The percentage values or fractions must be seen. It is possible to award (A0)(R1).</p>","er":""}],"notes":[]},{"id":"18M.1.SL.TZ1.T_6","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"18M","date":"May 2018","tz":"TZ1","legacy":"T_","marks":1,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>In a high school, 160 students completed a questionnaire which asked for the number of people they are following on a social media website. The results were recorded in the following box-and-whisker diagram.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>The following incomplete table shows the distribution of the responses from these 160 students.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Write down the mid-interval value for the 100 &lt; <i>x</i> ≤ 150 group.</p>","ms":"<p>125 (accept 125.5)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)</strong></em></p>","er":""}],"notes":[]},{"id":"19N.1.SL.TZ0.T_15","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"19N","date":"November 2019","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"T_","marks":6,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>Stephen was invited to perform a piano recital. In preparation for the event, Stephen recorded the amount of time, in minutes, that he rehearsed each day for the piano recital.</p><p>Stephen rehearsed for 32 days and data for all these days is displayed in the following box-and-whisker diagram.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>"},{"id":"c2","html":"<p>Stephen states that he rehearsed on each of the 32 days.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Write down the median rehearsal time.</p>","ms":"<p>42 (minutes)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)(C1)</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":2,"ctx":["c1","c2"],"q":"<p>State whether Stephen is correct. Give a reason for your answer.</p>","ms":"<p>Stephen is correct.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)</strong></em></p><p>the minimum rehearsal time is greater than zero&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(R1)</strong></em></p><p><strong>OR</strong></p><p>he rehearsed at least 20 minutes every day&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(R1)(C2)</strong></em></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Do not award (A1)(R0). Accept equivalent reasoning based on the box-and-whisker diagram.</p>","er":""},{"label":"c","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c1","c2"],"q":"<p>On <i>k</i> days, Stephen practiced exactly 24 minutes. Find the possible values of <i>k</i>.</p>","ms":"<p>0, 2, 3, 4, …, 15&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)(A1)(A1)(C3)</strong></em></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Award (A1)(A1) for each correct endpoint of the interval, (A1) for indication of integer values, except 1, between their endpoints.</p>","er":""}],"notes":[]},{"id":"20N.1.SL.TZ0.S_8","section":"B","paper":1,"session":"20N","date":"November 2020","tz":"TZ0","num":8,"legacy":"S_","marks":15,"context_status":"provided","contexts":[{"id":"context_6cd52210fe1137","html":"<p>Each athlete on a running team recorded the distance (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> miles) they ran in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> minutes.</p> <p>The median distance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> miles and the interquartile range is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.1</mn></math> miles.</p> <p>This information is shown in the following box-and-whisker plot.</p> <p style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>"},{"id":"context_c226e70cb16e2c","html":"<p>The distance in miles, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>, can be converted to the distance in kilometres, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>,&nbsp;using the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi></math>.</p>"},{"id":"context_4c69368772d5f9","html":"<p>The variance of the distances run by the athletes is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>km</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p> <p>The standard deviation of the distances is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> miles.</p>"},{"id":"context_9658a1b8a6a72f","html":"<p>A total of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn></math> athletes from different teams compete in a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mtext>km</mtext></math>&nbsp;race. The times the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn></math> athletes&nbsp;took to run the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mtext>km</mtext></math> race are shown in the following cumulative frequency graph.</p> <p><img style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p> <p>There were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn></math> athletes who took between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> minutes to complete the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mtext>km</mtext></math> race.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":2,"ctx":["context_6cd52210fe1137"],"q":"<p>Find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>.</p>","ms":"<p style=\"color:#999;font-size:90%;font-style:italic;\">* This question is from an exam for a previous syllabus, and may contain minor differences in marking or structure.</p><p>valid approach&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mn>4.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn></math></p> <p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.4</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>A1&nbsp; &nbsp;N2</strong></em></p> <p><em><strong>[2 marks]</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["context_6cd52210fe1137","context_c226e70cb16e2c"],"q":"<p>Write down the value of the median distance in kilometres (km).</p>","ms":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6.4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></math>&nbsp;(km)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>A1&nbsp; &nbsp;N1</strong></em></p> <p><em><strong>[1 mark]</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"c","type":"question","marks":4,"ctx":["context_6cd52210fe1137","context_c226e70cb16e2c","context_4c69368772d5f9"],"q":"<p>Find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>","ms":"<p><strong>METHOD 1 (standard deviation first)</strong></p> <p>valid approach&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>standard&nbsp;deviation</mtext><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mtext>variance</mtext></msqrt><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><msqrt><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p> <p>standard deviation<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(km)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)</strong></em></p> <p>valid approach to convert <strong>their</strong> standard deviation&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><msqrt><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi></math></p> <p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(miles)&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>A1&nbsp; &nbsp;N3</strong></em></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> If no working shown, award <em><strong>M1A1M0A0</strong></em> for the value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.<br>If working shown, and candidate’s final answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, award <em><strong>M1A1M0A0</strong></em>.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>METHOD 2 (variance first)</strong></p> <p>valid approach to convert variance&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p> <p>variance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)</strong></em></p> <p>valid approach&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>standard&nbsp;deviation</mtext><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mtext>variance</mtext></msqrt><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><msqrt><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><msqrt><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p> <p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></math> (miles)&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>A1&nbsp; &nbsp;N3</strong></em></p> <p><em><strong>[4 marks]</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"d","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["context_6cd52210fe1137","context_c226e70cb16e2c","context_4c69368772d5f9","context_9658a1b8a6a72f"],"q":"<p>Find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>.</p>","ms":"<p>correct frequency for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn></math> minutes &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math></p> <p>adding <strong>their</strong> frequency (do not accept <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn></math>)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mn>420</mn></math> athletes</p> <p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math>&nbsp;(minutes)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>A1&nbsp; &nbsp;N3</strong></em></p> <p><em><strong>[3 marks]</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"e","type":"question","marks":5,"ctx":["context_6cd52210fe1137","context_c226e70cb16e2c","context_4c69368772d5f9","context_9658a1b8a6a72f"],"q":"<p>The first <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn></math> athletes that completed the race won a prize.</p> <p>Given that an athlete took between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> minutes to complete the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mtext>km</mtext></math> race,&nbsp;calculate the probability that they won a prize.</p>","ms":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn></math>&nbsp;(minutes) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)</strong></em></p> <p>correct working<em><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (A1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>130</mn></math> athletes between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn></math> minutes,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>P</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>150</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mn>600</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></math></p> <p>evidence of conditional probability or reduced sample space &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<em><strong>(M1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>P</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mrow><mo lspace=\"0.1em\" rspace=\"0.1em\" stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mtext>P</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>27</mn><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mrow><mo lspace=\"0.1em\" rspace=\"0.1em\" stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mn>22</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mtext>P</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>P</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>150</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac></math></p> <p>correct working<em><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (A1)</strong></em></p> <p><em>eg</em>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>130</mn><mn>600</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mn>600</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>150</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mn>400</mn></mfrac></math></p> <p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>130</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.25em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>78000</mn><mn>240000</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>390</mn><mn>1200</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.325</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></math><em><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; A1&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;N5</strong></em></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> If no other working is shown, award <em><strong>A0A0M1A0A0</strong></em> for answer of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>150</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac></math>.<br>Award <em><strong>N0</strong></em> for answer of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> with no other working shown.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><em><strong>[5 marks]</strong></em></p>","er":""}]}]};
